{"family": "tapir", "task": "tracking", "name": "TAPIR", "plain": "TAPIR and BootsTAPIR (Google DeepMind, 2023 / 2024): track any point through a whole video offline: a per-frame match from a cost volume, then four temporal refinement passes; BootsTAPIR adds self-training on real videos. Apache-2.0 code and weights.", "summary": "TAPIR (Doersch, Yang, Vecerik et al., Google DeepMind 2023) and BootsTAPIR (Doersch et al. 2024, the same network trained further with BootsTAP self-training on unlabelled real videos): tracking any point offline over a whole video. A ResNet encodes every 256 x 256 frame; per frame, a cost volume against the query's features gives the initial position, visibility and uncertainty, then four PIPs-style refinements (local correlations, a depthwise-conv MLP mixer over the frames of each track) correct the whole track at once.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/tapnet", "upstream_commit": "ceedd60bb9f6c9f7c74796e4445aff6c6ddf7c9b", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "TAPIR: Tracking Any Point with per-frame Initialization and temporal Refinement", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08637", "date": "2023-06-14", "venue": "ICCV 2023", "variants": ["tapir"]}, {"title": "BootsTAP: Bootstrapped Training for Tracking-Any-Point", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.00847", "date": "2024-02-01", "venue": "ACCV 2024", "variants": ["bootstapir"]}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fvm_conv"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [], "outputs": [{"name": "tracks", "extra": false}, {"name": "visibility", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["Offline: the whole video is encoded before tracking (features of every frame in memory, about 3 MB per frame); for live video use an online tracker (TAPNext).", "Frames are resized to 256 x 256 (the training size and that of upstream's TAP-Vid numbers), whatever their size and aspect ratio. Upstream's higher-resolution refinement (best at 512 x 512 for BootsTAPIR) is not ported.", "One video per call; all queries of a call share the video."], "task_io": "Input: a video (its frames in order) and query points `(t, x, y)`. Output: the position of every query in every frame and the probability that it is visible there.", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "bootstapir", "released": "0.2.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "bootstapir@1", "name": "bootstapir", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "Apache-2.0", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "Apache-2.0", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/tapnet/blob/ceedd60bb9f6c9f7c74796e4445aff6c6ddf7c9b/README.md#license-and-disclaimer", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "Upstream: TAPIR is trained on synthetic Kubric MOVi-E sequences (the panning variant); BootsTAPIR is further trained with BootsTAP self-training on about 15 million unlabelled real video clips (not released). None has a dataset entry here yet.", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "bootstapir_checkpoint_v2.pt", "sha256": "8493c7a69e02c85b9382fbb3c7b8b539b36bc08ede744b9e99feb739a0129f4b", "size": 218886140, "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/dm-tapnet/bootstap/bootstapir_checkpoint_v2.pt", "host": "Google Drive", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 32, padded to a multiple of 32", "tested_max": {"size": "3000x4000", "alloc_mib": 5747, "reserved_mib": 6208}, "speed": {"standard": "480x854", "inputs": [{"input": "480x854", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": true, "modes": {"portable": {"ms": 232.86, "ms_min": 232.643, "noise": 